    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a heavy emphasis on exploiting the soft matchup against Mitch Spence, who carries an inflated 6.03 xERA. Consequently, our strongest play is **Kyle Tucker** (75.38), whose elite base projection and favorable pairing against Nick Martinez make him our anchor. He is closely followed by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), who benefits significantly from a +19% boost due to the opponent's SP skill and a high-leverage spot in the two-hole. **Andy Pages** (69.52) and **Nasim Nunez** (66.19) also emerge as core components of our offensive strategy; **Nasim Nunez** in particular serves as a vital spark plug for our scarce stolen base category, making his high efficiency score against a weak rotation particularly valuable for our Roto standing.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal utility slot, where **Josh Jung** (54.85) just missed the top-tier cut. While **Josh Jung** remains a high-upside asset, he was relegated to the bench in favor of the hot hand of **Wade Meckler** (58.29), whose matchup against Ryne Nelson offers better platoon utility and a more favorable batting order position. We are monitoring the status of **Liam Hicks** (45.31) closely; his projection is currently weighed down by a tough matchup against Zack Wheeler, and should his assumed leadoff spot be adjusted lower, we may see his efficiency drop near our critical \"below floor\" threshold. Aside from the ongoing injury management of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, the squad is healthy and positioned to capitalize on these specific SP vulnerabilities.",
